{"kind":"report","text":"Ready for review at exact clean head 4d1f4222e3ab5204c645ef785b0bfa170a1bd813 on task/mcp-repo-parameter-review-repair, with both changes-requested findings closed. Finding one, the stop path: main built its context with context.Background(), so an interrupt ended the process before the deferred withdrawal ran. I reproduced that at the reviewed head before changing anything, and the record survived the interrupt naming a dead process. main now derives the command context from signal.NotifyContext for interrupt and terminate, so an ordinary stop cancels the same context the serving path already watched, the withdrawal runs, and being told to stop is reported as success instead of as a server error. Finding two, the test gap: the existing test injected a cancellable context the command line never supplied. Two new tests build and run the real gs binary as a separate process and stop it with a real interrupt. One proves the advertisement is gone once the process has exited and that the exit reports success; the other starts a successor, stops the service it replaced, and proves the successor's advertisement survives and still answers, then that stopping the last one clears it. Each is mutation-checked: removing the signal handling, removing the withdrawal, or letting the closed-server error escape makes them fail. Declared scope beyond the findings: the reviewed head no longer merged into main, which had gained the MCP actor digest, so this is a fresh branch cut from main c95601d with the reviewed work carried across. The two meet in one place, and I changed it deliberately: the digest resolved the caller's fingerprint from a single attached workspace, which is wrong once a call can name any repository, so it now resolves from the room the call is acting in. Gates at this head: make vet, make test, go test -race ./..., go build ./..., make build, git diff --check, and a clean working tree.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c5